Two-line-scale change in core/mempool/src/lib.rs, no consensus surface touched.

(1) Close the fail-open hole at lib.rs:216-233 without introducing false rejects. Additionally require the sender's account object to exist, and treat an absent CoinStore on an otherwise-existing account as balance 0:

    if parsed_tx.paymaster.is_none() {
        if let Some(storage) = &self.storage {
            if storage.get_object(&parsed_tx.sender).is_none() {
                return Err("Unknown sender account".into());   // executor drops these anyway
            }
            if let Some(gas_cost) = (parsed_tx.gas_limit as u128).checked_mul(parsed_tx.gas_price) {
                let balance = executor::committed_ain_balance(storage, &parsed_tx.sender)
                    .unwrap_or(0);                              // absent store == 0, not "unknown"
                if balance < gas_cost { return Err(...); }
            }
        }
    }

This cannot false-reject anything the executor would have accepted: core/executor/src/lib.rs:2450 already drops unconditionally on a missing sender object, so a sender absent from committed state has no executable tx either way. Keep fail-open only for the genuinely ambiguous case (CoinStore bytes present but BCS-undecodable) by branching on decode failure rather than on key absence.

(2) Defense-in-depth on the auction itself, so admission is not the sole barrier — in `get_pending_transactions` (lib.rs:537-547), rank by `min(gas_price, committed_balance / gas_limit)` instead of raw `gas_price`, with an unreadable balance scoring 0. An unfunded tx may still be admitted but can never outbid a funded one for a block slot.

Add a regression test alongside core/mempool/src/tests.rs:765 (`ain_store_key`/`fund` helpers already exist): a never-funded sender declaring gas_price = u128::MAX must not be admitted, and must not preempt a funded sender at gas_price 1.

