Add a cumulative byte budget to the serve loop in sync/src/lib.rs:1054-1067, measured on the stored JSON (free — already read), always emitting at least one block so the requester still makes progress:

    const MAX_SYNC_RESP_BYTES: usize = 4 * 1024 * 1024; // well under read_encrypted_msg's 10 MiB frame cap
    let mut resp_bytes = 0usize;
    for height in (req.from_height + 1)..=end_height {
        let key = format!("block_{}", height);
        if let Ok(Some(block_data)) = self.storage.get(&key) {
            let sz = block_data.len();
            if !blocks_to_send.is_empty() && resp_bytes + sz > MAX_SYNC_RESP_BYTES {
                break; // byte budget reached; requester loops for the next batch
            }
            if let Ok(block) = serde_json::from_str::<Block>(&block_data) {
                resp_bytes += sz;
                blocks_to_send.push(block);
            }
        }
    }

The client loop already handles short batches correctly (it advances via `current = synced` at sync/src/lib.rs:687), so no client change is needed. Separately (follow-up, not part of this fix): a single block larger than 10 MiB would still be unsendable — cap total block payload bytes at production time in consensus/consensus/src/dag.rs:878-886, or charge per-byte gas in the executor, so no historical block can exceed the frame cap.

Track which connections were actually counted, and only decrement those. In the event loop (alongside `inbound_connections_by_host`, p2p.rs:247-248) add:

    let mut counted_inbound: std::collections::HashMap<libp2p::swarm::ConnectionId, String> = Default::default();

At the increment site (p2p.rs:345-347), record the id after incrementing: `counted_inbound.insert(connection_id, host.clone());`. At the close site (p2p.rs:370-378), replace the endpoint-derived host lookup with `if let Some(host) = counted_inbound.remove(&connection_id) { ... saturating_sub(1) ... }` (`ConnectionClosed` already carries `connection_id`; add it to the destructure at p2p.rs:367). This makes increment and decrement symmetric by construction and also self-heals the p2p.rs:348-357 rejection path. Equivalent alternative: move the per-host accounting above the per-peer guard at p2p.rs:318 so every inbound connection that reaches `ConnectionEstablished` is counted exactly once.

Before mainnet, gate creation to the system address — 1 line in core/vm_move/stdlib/sources/dex.move:63-64, mirroring the existing pattern at :57:

